From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: allow board-selected SGMII SFP host

Some copper SFP modules expose no PHY over I2C.  Allow a board to restrict
the PPE port to SGMII so the module's 1G in-band status is decoded instead
of selecting 2500BASE-X solely because it has the higher preference.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_port.c
@@ -1207,9 +1207,17 @@
 		MAC_SYM_PAUSE | MAC_10 | MAC_100 | MAC_1000 |
 		MAC_2500FD | MAC_5000FD | MAC_10000FD;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(mac_interfaces); i++)
-		__set_bit(mac_interfaces[i],
+	if (of_property_read_bool(ppe_port->np, "qcom,sfp-force-sgmii")) {
+		/* Some copper SFPs expose no PHY over I2C. Restrict this port to
+		 * SGMII when the board explicitly selects the 1G host path.
+		 */
+		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII,
 			  ppe_port->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
+	} else {
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(mac_interfaces); i++)
+			__set_bit(mac_interfaces[i],
+				  ppe_port->phylink_config.supported_interfaces);
+	}
 
 	/* Create phylink */
 	ppe_port->phylink = phylink_create(&ppe_port->phylink_config,
